From: Boot Time Experiment <boot-time@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] board: ti: j721e: skip SPL fixups without a payload DT

The Falcon firmware FIT has no A72 payload/control DT. spl_perform_fixups()
runs before k3_falcon_prep() loads the Linux FIT. Do not pass its NULL
fdt_addr into detect_enable_hyperflash(), where the selected GPIO state
could lead to a NULL FDT access. The existing K3 Falcon hook subsequently
prepares Linux bootargs and system DT fixups after loading the Linux DT.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 board/ti/j721e/evm.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/ti/j721e/evm.c b/board/ti/j721e/evm.c
--- a/board/ti/j721e/evm.c
+++ b/board/ti/j721e/evm.c
@@ -144,6 +144,10 @@
 void spl_perform_fixups(struct spl_image_info *spl_image)
 {
+	/* A firmware-only Falcon FIT has no payload device tree yet. */
+	if (!spl_image->fdt_addr)
+		return;
+
 	detect_enable_hyperflash(spl_image->fdt_addr);
 }
 #endif
 
